WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.270
-My first guest is a three-time
Grammy-winning artist.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:07.273
His concert film
"Magnificent Coloring World"

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:11.110
will be coming exclusively
to AMC Theatres this summer.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.614
Here he is, Chance the Rapper!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.649
Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about!

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.285
That's my friend. Come on, bud!

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.686
Looking great.
-Hey, man.

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:22.688
-Looking sharp, bud, as always.

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:23.823
Thanks so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:24.891
-Red carpet ready.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:25.992
Oh, thanks, man.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.393
-Yeah, please.
How are you doing?

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.061
How is the fam?
How are the kids?

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:31.230
-Everybody is good.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.399
We got --
My wife's in the other room.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:36.235
She's getting hair and makeup
and all types of stuff

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.538
ready for tonight's premiere.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.773
And the kids are
with their grandparents.

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.575
So it's going to be
a wild night.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.777
-Yeah. Good. I like wild nights.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:47.446
Look at how cute --
How old are they right now?

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:50.917
-That's Kensli and Marli.
They are five and two.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.118
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.120
-And they're into
the whole princess thing, huh?

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.189
-Yeah.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.357
I don't remember -- I think that
was, like, one of her friends

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:00.526
had, like,
an elaborate birthday party

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:01.894
where they were all princesses.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:06.199
So we went all out and got both
of them princess outfits.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.835
-Yeah. My girls dress like this
to go to school.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.237
[ Laughter ]
That's what they --

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.672
They just love it so much.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.307
I go, "Yeah, just go for it.
I don't care."

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.708
What are you gonna do?
-Yeah.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.109
-Last time you were on,
we talked about how much you --

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:18.477
your love of movies.

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:20.346
Are you showing the kids movies

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.282
like your favorite
when you were a kid?

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.749
-Oh, yeah. All the classics.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:27.519
My oldest daughter
is really into "Spy Kids,"

00:01:27.519 --> 00:01:29.122
which I don't know
if you remember "Spy Kids,"

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.589
but it was amazing.
-Yeah, I love "Spy Kids."

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:31.957
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:33.459
-It's great.
-Give it up for "Spy Kids."

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:37.063
It's amazing. And she
actually got hooked on it

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.398
because she found out about
Sharkboy and Lavagirl

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.267
from "We Can Be Heroes,"

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.436
which is a new movie on Netflix
that all the kids love.

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:46.305
But they don't know
it's connected to my childhood.

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:47.674
I grew up on
Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:50.677
-Wow!
-Pretty cool connection there.

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.011
Love of the films.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:55.147
-You are actually
doing a reboot,

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:57.083
I want to say, of "Home Alone."

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.551
Is that tr--
Did I read that right?

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.820
-[ Chuckles ]
It's a secret.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:04.490
I'm working on -- I got this
pitch for a "Home Alone" reboot.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.992
As a lot of people know --

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.661
I'm sure everybody here is
a huge fan of "Home Alone."

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.228
-Of course.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.197
-John Hughes.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.966
-Macaulay Culkin.
-Chicago guy.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.201
Yeah, Macaulay Culkin.
Chicago film.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.636
And since I was younger,
I always watched it.

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:21.107
And I was like, what if there
was a hood "Home Alone"?

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:23.475
Or "Hood Alone," if you will?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.475 --> 00:02:27.079
And just based -- just
a little more realistic story

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:29.348
about what happens
when people try

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:31.250
and kick in doors
at the wrong house.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:35.254
[ Laughter ]
And, you know, hilarity ensues.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:36.522
I can't give you
too many details,

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:37.823
but yeah,
thanks for saying that.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:41.628
Yes, hood "Home Alone."
-I like that. I like that.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:44.697
Is one -- Is one kid Kevin?

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.032
-There's two kids.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.634
But, uh, it's up for grabs.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:49.868
You want to get in
on this project?

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.004
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, I'm in.
Ground floor.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:55.040
I want to get in on
this "Hood Alone."

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.709
What are we calling it?
-[ Laughing ] "Hood Alone."

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.511
"Hood Alone."
Write it down, please.

00:02:59.511 --> 00:03:01.881
-I want to deal with
your production company,

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:05.450
which by the way, I love
the name -- House of Kicks.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.919
-House of Kicks. Yeah.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.721
-Was that sneakers? What is it?

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.189
-It's not. It's not sneakers.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.124
Why does everybody think it has
to do with shoes?

00:03:12.124 --> 00:03:14.727
So, it's House of Kicks.
It's my film house.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.629
It's where we make our movies
out of.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.399
And the name comes from
House of Kicks,

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:22.068
which was this black-owned
theme park

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.803
that all the kids in Chicago
used to go to.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:28.174
Like, all the day camps and
schools would take their kids

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.675
on field trips
to the House of Kicks.

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:34.113
It was this big indoor place
of wonder on the South Side

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.548
where there was not a lot of --
nothing that looked like that.

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:39.218
And when I first started
building, you know,

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:41.087
the film house
and getting into film stuff,

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:43.622
I wanted it to feel like
an amusement park.

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:45.892
So yep, House of Kicks --
no shoes involved.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.793
-No, yeah. I love that.

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:49.761
Yeah, you just want to have fun.
That's all.

00:03:49.761 --> 00:03:51.297
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.332
Thank you. Thank you, guys.

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:57.970
-You made this concert film,
which I'm a fan of.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.073
"The Magnificent
Coloring World."

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:02.908
-Yeah.
-What made you do it?

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:05.110
You shot this
a couple years ago, right?

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.112
-Yeah. I think I told you
about it when I first started.

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:09.015
So, basically
it's four years old.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:14.887
It was a film that I shot right
after I won the Grammys in 2017.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:19.091
I came back to Chicago right
after finishing up this tour,

00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:20.559
getting ready to go on
another one.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:24.263
And I just had this idea
that I wanted to do a concert

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.499
but specifically for film

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.834
and it'd be shot
like it was a movie

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.602
and eventually put it out
in theaters.

00:04:30.602 --> 00:04:33.606
And it came together
in like three weeks,

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:37.076
a bunch of years back,
and it was amazing.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.879
It was a beautiful experience,
but I didn't really know a lot

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:42.615
about film at all
or how to edit or anything.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:47.786
And so about three weeks ago,
I sent out for the film

00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:49.555
and brought it
to the studio house

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:52.091
and worked tirelessly on it
with about 20 people,

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:55.061
and, you know, shot some
new stuff, and also ended up

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.829
working out a partnership
with AMC Theatres

00:04:57.829 --> 00:04:59.498
to get it distributed.

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:03.936
And now I'm the first ever
independent distributor --

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:07.473
artist and distributor of a film
in AMC history.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.675
So things come together quickly
if you try hard.

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:10.709
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Right?

00:05:10.709 --> 00:05:12.377
-Get the right people.

00:05:12.377 --> 00:05:15.681
-By the way, I wanted to mention
how great you were

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:16.815
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:05:16.815 --> 00:05:19.285
I thought you were fantastic
when you hosted.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.285
-Thank you, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:21.720
-Talented dude.
-I appreciate it.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.456
-Talented guy.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.524
Here's a peek at
"Magnificent Coloring World."

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:26.692
Take a look at this.

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.661
